      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "word = input()\neat_left = True\nresult = \"\"\nwhile word:\n    letter = word[0] if eat_left else word[-1]\n    word = word[1:] if eat_left else word[:-1]\n    result += letter\n    if letter in \"aeiou\":\n        eat_left = not eat_left\nprint(result)\n",
      "statement": "A caterpillar eats [[word]], one letter at a time, starting at its <<left end>>. Each eaten letter is removed.\n\n<<After eating a vowel>>, it switches to the other end of the remaining word. After eating a consonant, it keeps eating from the same end.\n\nThe vowels are {{a}}, {{e}}, {{i}}, {{o}} and {{u}}. Every other letter, including {{y}}, is a consonant.\n\nPrint all letters in the order they are eaten.",
